  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Nicodemus (John 3:1-2) and Gamaliel (Acts 5:34-39) were both Pharisees. How do their stories complicate the picture of the Pharisees as simply Jesus's enemies?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Jesus's sharpest warnings were aimed at devout, Bible-loving people. Where might Matthew 23:23-28 speak to our own church life today?" .
