  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Jewish movement of the Second Temple period known for careful interpretation and practice of the Torah, the \"tradition of the elders\" and belief in the resurrection; Jesus's frequent conversation partners and critics in the Gospels, Paul's own party, and forerunners of the later rabbis." .
